      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>National University Student Organization (NUSO) is a supporting agency to National University and provides services to students in support of National University's academic mission.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>NUSO administers and oversees student organizations, programs, and co-curricular activities at various National University campuses, affiliates, and for any online programs. The individual Student Organizations created, administered, and overseen by NUSO shall be student interest groups that exist for the benefit and enrichment of the student experience at National University. There are 909 students being served by 16 student organizations. The office fosters community and belonging via intentional programming of webinars and events for students. The office hosts the Student Voice blog, written by club officers, and administers various aspects of student life for adult learners, including mentoring and supporting student events.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
